 also is a dominant factor. There are four major glaciers in the country, including the largest glacier in Europe, Vatnajökull, which is around 8,300 square kilometers (3,200 square miles) in size.\'  Given Iceland\'s status as a Commonwealth at the time, we have chosen to treat the natural boundaries of the island as coextensive with its political borders.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 884, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 825})
